## Variable not bound in every alternative of a pattern test

```catala
declaration enumeration E:
  -- A content integer
  -- B content integer
  -- F

declaration scope S:
  context e content E
  output o content boolean

scope S:
  definition e equals A content 1
  definition o equals e with pattern (A content x or F) and x > 0
```

```catala-test-cli
$ catala test-scope S
┌─[ERROR]─
│
│  The variable x is bound in pattern A but not in pattern F.
│
├─➤ tests/enum/bad/or_pattern_test_unbound_var.catala_en:15.49-50:
│    │
│ 15 │   definition o equals e with pattern (A content x or F) and x > 0
│    │                                                 ‾
├─ Variable not bound in every alternative of a pattern test
│
├─➤ tests/enum/bad/or_pattern_test_unbound_var.catala_en:15.54-55:
│    │
│ 15 │   definition o equals e with pattern (A content x or F) and x > 0
│    │                                                      ‾
└─ Variable not bound in every alternative of a pattern test
#return code 123#
```
